    "question": "An aqueous solution of metal nitrate 'P' reacts with potassium iodide solution to give a bright yellow precipitate 'Q'. On heating 'P' strongly in a dry test tube, a yellow solid residue 'R', a reddish-brown gas 'S', and a gas 'T' that rekindles a glowing splinter are obtained.\n(a) Identify P, Q, R, S, and T.\n(b) Write balanced chemical equations for both reactions.",
    "answer": "(a) Identification of Substances:\n- **P:** Lead nitrate, $Pb(NO_3)_2$\n- **Q:** Lead iodide, $PbI_2$ (Bright yellow precipitate)\n- **R:** Lead(II) oxide / Litharge, $PbO$ (Yellow solid residue)\n- **S:** Nitrogen dioxide, $NO_2$ (Pungent brown gas)\n- **T:** Oxygen gas, $O_2$ (Colorless gas rekindling glowing splinter)\n\n(b) Balanced Chemical Equations:\n1. **Precipitation Reaction:**\n$$Pb(NO_3)_2(aq) + 2KI(aq) \\rightarrow PbI_2(s) \\downarrow [\\text{Yellow ppt}] + 2KNO_3(aq)$$\n\n2. **Thermal Decomposition Reaction:**\n$$2Pb(NO_3)_2(s) \\xrightarrow{\\Delta} 2PbO(s) + 4NO_2(g) \\uparrow + O_2(g) \\uparrow$$",
