    "answer": "(a) Identification:\n- **X:** Copper metal ($Cu$, reddish-brown)\n- **Y:** Copper(II) oxide ($CuO$, black)\n- **Z:** Water ($H_2O$, liquid)\n\n(b) Balanced Chemical Equations:\n1. **Oxidation of Copper:**\n$$2Cu(s) + O_2(g) \\xrightarrow{\\Delta} 2CuO(s) [\\text{Black Surface}]$$\n\n2. **Reduction of Copper(II) Oxide with Hydrogen:**\n$$CuO(s) [\\text{Black}] + H_2(g) \\xrightarrow{\\Delta} Cu(s) [\\text{Reddish-Brown}] + H_2O(l)$$\n\n(c) Redox Analysis of Reaction 2:\n- **Substance Oxidised:** Hydrogen ($H_2$) [Gains oxygen to form $H_2O$]\n- **Substance Reduced:** Copper(II) oxide ($CuO$) [Loses oxygen to form $Cu$]\n- **Oxidising Agent:** Copper(II) oxide ($CuO$) [Provides oxygen]\n- **Reducing Agent:** Hydrogen ($H_2$) [Removes oxygen from $CuO$]\n\n(d) Commercial Application of Metal 'X' (Copper):\nCopper is highly ductile and an excellent conductor of electricity; it is used extensively for electrical wiring, electric motors, power transmission cables, and cooking utensil bases.",
