    "answer": "(a) Reaction:\n$$2HNO_3(aq) + Ca(OH)_2(aq) \\rightarrow Ca(NO_3)_2(aq) + 2H_2O(l)$$\n- **Classification:** Double displacement / Acid-Base Neutralisation.\n\n(b) Reaction:\n$$2NaOH(aq) + H_2SO_4(aq) \\rightarrow Na_2SO_4(aq) + 2H_2O(l)$$\n- **Classification:** Double displacement / Acid-Base Neutralisation.\n\n(c) Reaction:\n$$NaCl(aq) + AgNO_3(aq) \\rightarrow AgCl(s) \\downarrow [\\text{White ppt}] + NaNO_3(aq)$$\n- **Classification:** Double displacement and Precipitation.\n\n(d) Reaction:\n$$BaCl_2(aq) + H_2SO_4(aq) \\rightarrow BaSO_4(s) \\downarrow [\\text{White ppt}] + 2HCl(aq)$$\n- **Classification:** Double displacement and Precipitation.\n\n(e) Reaction:\n$$3Fe(s) + 4H_2O(g) \\rightarrow Fe_3O_4(s) + 4H_2(g)$$\n- **Classification:** Single displacement / Redox reaction. *(Note: Water is gaseous steam).*",
    "explanation": "Reason: Balancing maintains stoichiometric conservation of all participating elements.",
